📁 Dataset — HIT-UAV
HIT-UAV (Suo et al., 2022) is ahigh-altitude infrared thermal dataset for UAVs:

2,898 images extracted from 43,470 frames (train 2,008 / val 287 / test 603)
5 classes: Person, Car, Bicycle, OtherVehicle, DontCare
Flight altitude: 60–130 m · camera pitch: 30–90° · day and night
Scenes: schools, parking lots, roads, playgrounds
Used in pre-converted YOLO format (class_id x_center y_center width height)
⚙️ Pipeline
Data acquisition — dataset pulled programmatically via kagglehub into Colab
Label integrity check — visualized ground-truth boxes over images before training to catchformat/path/class-order errors early
Config normalization — rewrote dataset.yaml with absolute paths and verified class index mapping
Transfer learning — YOLOv8n fine-tuned from COCO weights (Bicycle/Car/Person head weights transferred directly)
Evaluation — mAP on held-out splits, per-class breakdown, confusion matrix analysis
Threshold analysis — tested conf thresholds 0.15–0.4 to map the precision/recall trade-off for small-object recall
